{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"3c09eeca-eaac-4699-a301-80ead1c27e49","step":{"id":"s1","script":"On the unit circle, an angle selects a point. Its vertical coordinate is sine; the graph records that height against the angle.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"circle","region":"left","frame":{"x":[-1.4,1.4],"y":[-1.4,1.4],"axes":"origin","equal_scale":true,"x_label":"x","y_label":"y"},"marks":[{"kind":"circle","id":"unit","center":[0,0],"r":1},{"kind":"point","id":"center","at":[0,0]},{"kind":"point","id":"start","at":[1,0],"label":"0"},{"kind":"segment","id":"radius","from":{"at":"center"},"to":{"at":"start"},"label":"1"}]},{"op":"figure","id":"wave","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-0.2,6.6],"y":[-1.4,1.4],"axes":"edge","x_label":"θ (radians)","y_label":"sin θ"},"marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"wave_start","at":[0,0],"label":"0"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"height_rule","anchor":{"el":"circle","side":"below","gap":0.04},"latex":"(x,y)=(\\cos\\theta,\\sin\\theta)"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"3c09eeca-eaac-4699-a301-80ead1c27e49","step":{"id":"s2","script":"At thirty degrees, the point is half a unit high. Plot that same height at pi over six; continuing the rotation traces a sine wave.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"circle_angle","on":"circle","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"p30","at":[0.8660254,0.5]},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"center"},"to":{"at":"p30"},"arrow":true},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"p30"},"to":[0,0.5],"stroke":"dashed","label":"½"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"p30"},"to":[0.8660254,0],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"angle","at":{"at":"center"},"from":{"at":"start"},"to":{"at":"p30"},"r":0.25,"label":"θ"}]},{"op":"figure","id":"trace_wave","on":"wave","marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"sine","y":"sin(x)","domain":[0,6.283185307]},{"kind":"point","id":"wave30","at":{"on":"sine","x":0.523598776},"label":"½"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"wave30"},"to":[0.523598776,0],"stroke":"dashed"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"sample","anchor":{"el":"height_rule","side":"below","gap":0.04},"latex":"\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)=\\frac12"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"3c09eeca-eaac-4699-a301-80ead1c27e49","step":{"id":"s3","script":"A quarter turn reaches the top of the circle. Its height is one, so the sine wave reaches its maximum at pi over two.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"circle_top","on":"circle","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"top","at":[0,1],"label":"1"},{"kind":"arc","center":{"at":"center"},"r":1.12,"start":0,"end":90,"arrow":true}]},{"op":"figure","id":"wave_peak","on":"wave","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"peak","at":{"on":"sine","x":1.570796327},"label":"1"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"peak"},"to":[1.570796327,0],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"text","at":[1.570796327,-0.22],"text":"π/2","size":"small"}]}],"checkpoint":{"question":"After half a turn, what is the point's height and therefore the sine value?","expected_gist":"Both are zero at θ = π."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"3c09eeca-eaac-4699-a301-80ead1c27e49","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Half a turn gives zero; three quarters gives minus one. A full turn returns to the start, so the sine wave repeats every two pi.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"circle_cycle","on":"circle","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"half","at":[-1,0],"label":"π"},{"kind":"point","id":"bottom","at":[0,-1],"label":"−1"},{"kind":"arc","center":{"at":"center"},"r":1.12,"start":90,"end":350,"arrow":true}]},{"op":"figure","id":"wave_cycle","on":"wave","marks":[{"kind":"point","at":{"on":"sine","x":3.141592654},"label":"π"},{"kind":"point","id":"trough","at":{"on":"sine","x":4.71238898},"label":"−1"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"trough"},"to":[4.71238898,0],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"text","at":[4.71238898,0.2],"text":"3π/2","size":"small"},{"kind":"point","at":{"on":"sine","x":6.283185307},"label":"2π"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"period","anchor":{"el":"wave","side":"below","gap":0.04},"latex":"\\sin(\\theta+2\\pi)=\\sin\\theta"}],"checkpoint":null}}
